{
  "title": "AudioStream",
  "description": "A live or unbounded audio source, such as internet radio. Readiness means playback can start: a live source never finishes downloading. Its duration may be `Infinity`, seeking is only available when the source reports a seekable range, and the connection can break and recover while the stream exists. connection and onConnectionChange report that health separately from playback. When the connection breaks - a network error, or the server ending the response of a live source - a URL-backed stream reopens the URL with exponential backoff, and a voice that was playing resumes once data arrives. After the configured attempts it reports `'disconnected'` and dispatches onError. reconnect starts a new round manually. Load it with `assets.load([AudioStream, 'https://radio.example/stream'])`. Use Music for a finite track.",
  "symbol": "AudioStream",
  "kind": "class",
  "subsystem": "audio",
  "importPath": "@codexo/exojs",
  "tier": "stable",
